<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

  <!--
    RUST_CATHEDRAL_MECHANICS_1 §4 — makes the Cathedral's canals fishable, with
    exactly one fish in them.

    RUT_RustCathedral is owned by mandrake.rut.patches (Defs/BiomeDefs/
    RUT_RustCathedral.xml) and ships with NEITHER maxFishPopulation NOR
    fishTypes. This mod already declares loadAfter mandrake.rut.patches, so a
    PatchOperationAdd lands after the biome exists.

    🔴 maxFishPopulation is NOT cosmetic and NOT optional — the kit spec flagged
    it as a ❓ and the answer is that it is currently ZERO (BiomeDef.cs:141
    defaults it to 0 and the Cathedral def never sets it). At zero:
      - WaterBodyTracker.cs:90 skips its whole population tick, so eels never
        regrow, and
      - Zone_Fishing.cs:82 refuses to be a fishing zone at all.
    Without this line §4 is dead content. INVENTED: 150. Vanilla's lowest
    non-zero is ExtremeDesert at 240 and Scarlands/Space are flat 0; 150 puts
    the canals below every real biome without switching fishing off.

    ⚠️ Even with this set, a canal must be physically large for fish to appear:
    WaterBody.SetFishTypes rolls
    FishingUtility.ChanceForCommonFishFromWaterBodySizeCurve, which is 0 below
    75 cells and does not reach 1.0 until 200. A narrow authored canal may hold
    no fish at all. That is map geometry, not a def bug — flagged, not patched.

    🔑 fishTypes uses a LoadDataFromXmlCustom list (FishChance.cs): the entry
    form is <DefName>weight</DefName>, NEVER <li>. An <li> here silently
    discards the WHOLE BiomeDef.

    THE ODYSSEY GATE IS AN XPATH TEST, not MayRequire and not
    PatchOperationFindMod, and the reason is specific:
      - MayRequire on an <Operation> node is INERT. LoadedModManager.cs:395
        honours it for DEF nodes only; ModContentPack.LoadPatches (:357-385)
        loads every <Operation> child unconditionally and never looks at
        attributes. Checked in source, not assumed.
      - PatchOperationFindMod matches on ModLister.HasActiveModWithName, i.e.
        About.xml's <name> — and Odyssey's About.xml has NO <name> element at
        all (only packageId Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey), so that route depends on
        a fallback display name rather than an identifier.
    Testing for FishBase — the Odyssey abstract this mod's eel inherits from,
    in the very document being patched — is exact and needs no name at all.
    Without Odyssey, RUT_CoolantEel's own def node is MayRequire'd away (which
    IS honoured), so skipping this patch leaves nothing dangling. Both BiomeDef
    fields are core, so the cost of skipping is zero.

    freshwater_Common only, by design:
      - the eel is the SOLE entry, so every canal catch is an eel (spec: "sole
        entry in the Cathedral biome's fishTypes"),
      - saltwater_* stay absent, so any salt body on a Cathedral map has no
        fish whatsoever — "canal water bodies only",
      - freshwater_Uncommon stays absent so the 5% uncommon roll finds nothing
        and falls through to the eel,
      - rareCatchesSetMaker stays absent: the spec defers the canal rare-catch
        table to a later content pass, and leaving it null makes vanilla's 1%
        rare branch unreachable rather than rolling some other biome's table.
  -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <!-- Gate 1: Odyssey is in the load set (see the note above). -->
    <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[@Name="FishBase"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationConditional">
      <!-- Gate 2: degrade to a silent no-op rather than a red error every
           launch if mandrake.rut.patches (which owns RUT_RustCathedral) is
           inactive, or if it ever ships these two fields itself. -->
      <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RUT_RustCathedral" and not(fishTypes)]</xpath>
      <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
        <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RUT_RustCathedral"]</xpath>
        <value>
          <maxFishPopulation>150</maxFishPopulation>
          <fishTypes>
            <freshwater_Common>
              <RUT_CoolantEel>1</RUT_CoolantEel>
            </freshwater_Common>
          </fishTypes>
        </value>
      </match>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
